{"id":"double-hold-42","name":"Double hold (42)","chapter":"Tricks in one count / Brolly notation","kind":"pattern","page":32,"label":"31","jugglers":null,"objects":null,"timing":null,"pdf":"https://www.jugglingedge.com/pdf/highgate.pdf#page=32&view=FitH,666","passist":null,"notations":[{"type":"hg-siteswap-in-title","value":"42"}],"derived":null,"body":[{"t":"p","h":"One well known three object siteswap is 42. In Brolly notation, since a 3 is a half spin zap in five club one count, then a 4 is a single pass. Any throw less than a 3 is the same as it would be in a solo siteswap pattern. So the 2 is a hold. So at any time in five club one count, one person can throw a single pass followed by a hold."},{"t":"d","i":0},{"t":"p","h":"In the diagram Ben throws a crossing right hand single pass followed by a left hand hold. Anne gets a hold in her pattern. Note that Ben&#x27;s zaps are straight, so his single pass is crossing. Anne&#x27;s zaps are crossing, so if she does this trick, she throws a straight single pass."}],"drawings":[{"file":"p32-1.png","kind":"causal diagram","reading":{"rows":[{"juggler":"A","name":"Anne","offset":0.0,"tempo":1.0,"beats":[{"t":0.0,"hand":"R"},{"t":1.0,"hand":"L"},{"t":2.0,"hand":"R"},{"t":3.0,"hand":"L"},{"t":4.0,"hand":"R"},{"t":5.0,"hand":"L"},{"t":6.0,"hand":"R"},{"t":7.0,"hand":"L"},{"t":8.0,"hand":"R"}]},{"juggler":"B","name":"Ben","offset":0.5,"tempo":1.0,"beats":[{"t":0.5,"hand":"R"},{"t":1.5,"hand":"L"},{"t":2.5,"hand":"R"},{"t":3.5,"hand":"L"},{"t":4.5,"hand":"R"},{"t":5.5,"hand":"L"},{"t":6.5,"hand":"R"},{"t":7.5,"hand":"L"}]}],"arrows":[{"from":[0,0.0,"R"],"to":[1,0.5,"R"]},{"from":[0,1.0,"L"],"to":[1,1.5,"L"]},{"from":[0,2.0,"R"],"to":[1,2.5,"R"]},{"from":[0,4.0,"R"],"to":[1,4.5,"R"]},{"from":[0,5.0,"L"],"to":[1,5.5,"L"]},{"from":[0,6.0,"R"],"to":[1,6.5,"R"]},{"from":[0,7.0,"L"],"to":[1,7.5,"L"]},{"from":[1,1.5,"L"],"to":[0,2.0,"R"]},{"from":[1,4.5,"R"],"to":[0,5.0,"L"]},{"from":[1,5.5,"L"],"to":[0,6.0,"R"]},{"from":[1,7.5,"L